  "title": "Unusual Sessions",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "bf2af98d-dccc-4e7f-83aa-bc1d18bc4064",
      "question": "Treat January 2 through June 30, 2026 as the baseline for every issuer. Which 10 issuer sessions from July 1 through August 31, 2026 were the most unusual in return, volatility and volume, and which features made each one unusual? Anomaly scores are neither forecasts nor explanations.",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T21:02:44.434341Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T21:04:13.704879Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Top‑10 most unusual issuer sessions (Jul 1 – Aug 31 2026)**\n*Baseline: Jan 2 – Jun 30 2026.  Anomaly scores are robust‑z‑score combinations; they are not forecasts or causal explanations.  “Observed deviations” are robust z‑scores for each feature (not raw returns or percentages).*\n\n| Rank | Asset | Session (UTC) | Anomaly Score | Features driving the anomaly (robust z‑scores) |\n|------|-------|---------------|--------------|-----------------------------------------------|\n| 1 | **DREI** | 2026‑07‑08 | 16.56 | 1‑day return **‑25.96**, 5‑day return **‑11.56**, 20‑day volatility **+14.41**, volume deviation **+14.81** |\n| 2 | **MOST** | 2026‑07‑27 | 15.04 | 5‑day return **+10.24**, 20‑day volatility **+12.42**, 1‑day return **‑2.53**, volume deviation **+0.88** |\n| 3 | **DREI** | 2026‑07‑09 | 14.98 | 20‑day volatility **+14.41**, 5‑day return **‑11.44**, 1‑day return **+0.95**, volume deviation **+0.37** |\n| 4 | **FLOA** | 2026‑07‑02 | 13.64 | 5‑day return **+9.91**, 20‑day volatility **+12.49**, 1‑day return **‑2.42**, volume deviation **‑0.58** |\n| 5 | **DREI** | 2026‑07‑14 | 12.93 | 20‑day volatility **+14.36**, 5‑day return **‑10.89**, 1‑day return **+0.61**, volume deviation **+0.60** |\n| 6 | **DREI** | 2026‑07‑10 | 11.62 | 20‑day volatility **+14.33**, 5‑day return **‑11.80**, 1‑day return **‑1.13**, volume deviation **+0.27** |\n| 7 | **MOST** | 2026‑07‑21 | 11.56 | 1‑day return **+23.62**, volume deviation **+13.86**, 5‑day return **+8.72**, 20‑day volatility **+12.19** |\n| 8 | **FLOA** | 2026‑07‑01 | 10.86 | 5‑day return **+11.29**, 20‑day volatility **+12.31**, 1‑day return **+0.49**, volume deviation **‑1.13** |\n| 9 | **REXI** | 2026‑07‑06 | 10.64 | 20‑day volatility **+12.78**, 5‑day return **+9.17**, 1‑day return **‑1.71**, volume deviation **‑0.61** |\n|10| **DREI** | 2026‑07‑13 | 10.57 | 20‑day volatility **+14.32**, 5‑day return **‑12.25**, 1‑day return **‑2.10**, volume deviation **+1.05** |\n\n**How the features made each session unusual**\n- **Adjusted 1‑day return** (`adjusted_return_1d`): large positive or negative z‑scores indicate a single‑day price move far outside the Jan‑Jun baseline.\n- **Adjusted 5‑day return** (`adjusted_return_5d`): captures multi‑day momentum that deviates strongly from the baseline distribution.\n- **Realized 20‑day volatility** (`realized_volatility_20d`): high positive z‑scores mean the rolling volatility over the prior 20 sessions was far above normal.\n- **Log volume deviation** (`log_volume_deviation_20d`): high absolute z‑scores show trading volume far above (or below) its recent 20‑session norm.\n\nEach flagged session combines several of these extreme deviations, producing the highest anomaly scores in the scoring window.\n\n**Limitations** – The tool’s output notes that anomaly scores describe unusual observed feature combinations only; they are not forecasts or probabilities, and observed deviations are robust z‑scores, not raw returns or percentages.  They do not establish cause or adverse events.\n\n[1]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — market anomaly scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:6030be60c38c80506f8c24b063a30f0d6cbd7b0a8aa4cd49d77c819803ca00a4`",
